nce; (2) a generic token-boundary/quantity-parser correction so technical designations cannot be clipped; (3) separately, a conservative intent route for unambiguous service-only work or non-catalog consumables; (4) only if simpler normalization fails, runtime manufacturer/model enrichment for repeated branded families.', 'decision_impact': 'Prefer testing retrieval-only supplier/model-noise de-emphasis, with the untouched original query retained and no inferred specifications or final-selection changes. It targets a repeated 35-row class and differs from the previously rejected endpoint/inch expansion. Treat the designation-truncation repair as a small correctness fix or separate experiment. Keep service/consumable abstention isolated: some work lines include an underlying product, and prior selection-adjacent changes were risky.', 'unresolved': 'The review-pool gzip remains CRC-corrupt, though its intended set is exactly reconstructable from the other supplied files. Branded model strings may encode material, porting, or connection details not stated elsewhere; a de-emphasis alternate must therefore be additive and preserve all explicit non-model tokens. Filter rows need a product-vs-consumable distinction before any NOT_FOUND routing.', 'sources': [], 'origin': 'attempt-02-research-first', 'kind': 'research-first'}, {'question': 'What recurring real-tender failure classes and bounded directions should inform the next hypothesis?', 'findings': 'The intact corpus reconstructs the 130 review rows (253 total minus 90 labelled minus 33 provisional NOT_FOUND); the supplied review-pool gzip remains CRC-corrupt. The largest viable-looking unresolved class is branded threaded ball valves: 53 ball-valve rows, 42 with third-party brands, including 30 IVR rows. Current canonicalization emits an alternate for only 40/130 review rows, and none for representative IVR/VALTEC rows. Official manufacturer data shows the opaque IVR 954/956 codes carry material retrieval facts: full-bore threaded ball valve and F/F versus M/F endpoints; VALTEC VT.214 likewise identifies a ball valve with an internal-thread endpoint. LD has hundreds of brass threaded ball-valve products, including explicit В-В/В-Н and handle variants, so this is a real vocabulary/underspecification gap—not evidence that foreign branded products are automatically interchangeable with LD.\n\nA separate correctness defect is confirmed: the clause terminator treats the embedded «ШТ.» in a technical designation as a quantity token, reducing «Кран БИВАЛ КШТ.11.050.025.ф/ф 50х25 КОФ» to «Кран БИВАЛ К». This should be repaired by token-boundary parsing, not a designation-specific rule. The pool also contains 33 filter/water-treatment rows and explicit work rows; many are consumables or service requests, but a few service lines embed a product, so broad abstention is unsafe.\n\nPromising directions: (1) a bounded, fail-open runtime manufacturer/model enrichment path for extractable brand+model queries, using a trusted manufacturer source and adding only explicitly documented generic facts to an alternate retrieval query; retain the original query and final selection semantics. (2) A small generic quantity/clause-boundary correction that preserves technical designations in retrieval alternates. (3) A later conservative product-intent/uncertainty route restricted to unambiguous service-only or consumable-only queries. Do not repeat deterministic inch/endpoint expansion or generic supplier-token suppression: both have already been rejected by hidden safety gates.', 'decision_impact': 'The strongest new product opportunity is source-backed, additive enrichment of repeated branded model nomenclature, because a model code can resolve endpoint and bore facts that the tender omits. It has external dependency, latency, caching, and source-trust costs, and must never assert LD equivalence or override reranking. If the Planner wants the lowest-risk bounded experiment instead, select the generic des