{"question":"What causal mechanisms remain credible after evidence synthesis for Harness v2 attempt 2?","findings":"The current path is raw-query retrieval plus at most one canonical alternate, merged per modality by its single best variant rank, then RRF top-20 and reranking against the untouched raw query. In the reconstructed 130-row review set, 69 mention valves/cranes, 52 have threaded/inch cues, 39 contain third-party brand cues, 33 concern filters/water treatment, and 11 are explicit service actions; only 40 rows receive a canonical alternate. The catalog has 15,788 products with extensive ball-valve (14,428) and butterfly-valve (356) coverage, but no IVR/VALTEC/TECOFI, cartridge, or water-treatment terminology; its 129 filter entries are not cartridge/water-treatment products. A real parser defect is confirmed: an embedded technical-designation substring “КШТ.” is treated as a quantity boundary and reduces one review query to “Кран БИВАЛ К”. This is a generic boundary error, but only one affected review row was observed, so its expected direct corpus value is limited. There is no new evidence for another branded-token suppression, threaded/inch semantic expansion, or manufacturer enrichment refinement: all three evaluated attempts raised hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND rates.","decision_impact":"The main decision is whether unresolved value is primarily lost inside the accepted alternate-query retrieval mechanism, or whether a substantial portion of the corpus is genuinely outside LD’s catalog scope and needs honest uncertainty. Do not infer that more semantic expansion is the bottleneck: repeated branded-query transformations were unsafe. A bounded experiment should discriminate evidence-preservation/fusion from non-catalog intent while retaining raw retrieval and guarding against wrong NOT_FOUND.","unresolved":"The review set is intentionally unresolved, so its class counts show opportunity rather than end-to-end uplift. The raw query remains active, so the parser defect may not affect final candidate availability. The supplied review-pool gzip remains corrupt, although its 130 intended rows are exactly reconstructable from the intact all-row, label, and provisional-NOT_FOUND files.","sources":[],"evidence_patterns":[{"pattern":"Semantics-preserving retrieval canonicalization is the only repeatedly validated mechanism, while added domain semantics do not reliably improve end-to-end outcomes.","supporting_experiments":["Legacy cycles 3 and 4 were accepted for additive deterministic canonicalization, including standalone WW translation.","Legacy cycle 6 flanged-shorthand expansion regressed blind safety; cycle 9 standard-bore expansion was neutral; cycle 17 actuation-state expansion was rejected."],"interpretation":"The supported causal path is preserving or translating unambiguous evidence into catalog vocabulary, not completing underspecified technical meaning. The confirmed embedded-quantity boundary error directly damages that established path, but its observed prevalence is low.","confidence":0.95},{"pattern":"Genericizing branded nomenclature or importing manufacturer facts repeatedly increased hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND despite retaining raw-query retrieval.","supporting_experiments":["Attempt 1 threaded/inch expansion: hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND +0.04.","Attempt 2 supplier/model-noise suppression: hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND +0.04.","Attempt 3 trusted manufacturer/model enrichment: hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND +0.08."],"interpretation":"Third-party model strings identify a recurring corpus class, but the causal bottleneck is not merely lexical noise or absent source-product facts. Foreign-product facts do not establish an appropriate LD equivalent; this mechanism family is locally saturated absent materially new evidence.","confidence":0.97},{"pattern":"Interventions that filter, alter candidate composition, or influence final selection have not produced a safe gain.","supporting_experiments":["Legacy cycles 1–2 broad gating/compatibility intervention regressed.","Legacy cycle 5 reranker rubric regressed; cycle 8 post-rerank compatibility fallback was neutral.","Legacy cycle 7 catalog structural enrichment reduced hidden coverage; cycle 16 candidate diversification reduced public coverage."],"interpretation":"Selection-adjacent changes are not categorically impossible, but they require a separable affirmative signal. Generic compatibility, candidate pruning, prompt tightening, and catalog-derived structure are weakly supported causal levers in this system.","confidence":0.92},{"pattern":"The unresolved corpus contains a materially distinct non-catalog or service-like segment.","supporting_experiments":["Review-corpus inspection found 33 filter/water-treatment rows and 11 explicit service-action rows.","Catalog inspection found zero cartridge/ЭФГ and water-treatment terms, while its filter products are primarily industrial грязевики.","Examples include cartridge filters, mixed-action filter disassembly/repair, and water de-ironing installations."],"interpretation":"For many such requests, broader retrieval cannot create a compatible sellable LD product. However, some service text embeds a concrete product request, so action words or the word “filter” alone are not sufficient grounds for NOT_FOUND.","confidence":0.9},{"pattern":"Alternate-query evidence is discarded before cross-modality fusion.","supporting_experiments":["Current HybridRetriever retrieves raw and canonical variants, then _merge_modality_candidates retains only the best per-candidate rank within dense and within BM25 before RRF.","40 of 130 review rows currently receive a canonical alternate."],"interpretation":"A candidate corroborated by raw and canonical wording receives no extra RRF evidence beyond its stronger hit. This is an untested architectural implication of the accepted canonicalization mechanism, distinct from adding another semantic alias; its benefit remains unmeasured.","confidence":0.88}],"candidate_directions":[{"mechanism_family":"query_evidence_preservation","history_relation":"REFINEMENT","causal_mechanism":"Repair structural clause/quantity boundary recognition so canonical retrieval alternates cannot terminate inside an alphanumeric designation, while preserving raw retrieval, existing transformations, and reranking behavior.","competing_explanation":"Raw-query retrieval already provides the required candidate, and the one observed damaged designation may have no material effect on the final top-20.","falsifier":"On a stratified set of affected technical-designation rows, corrected alternates neither improve viable family-consistent candidate presence/rank nor provide an end-to-end real-tender value signal while guardrails remain flat.","information_gain":"Moderate. It isolates a confirmed correctness failure within the one successful mechanism family, but the observed affected population is small and should not be overstated."},{"mechanism_family":"query_variant_evidence_fusion","history_relation":"NEW_LAYER","causal_mechanism":"Preserve raw-query and canonical-query hits as separate retrieval-evidence channels through fusion, rewarding cross-variant corroboration without removing candidates or changing reranker inputs/selection semantics.","competing_explanation":"Canonical alternates may mostly retrieve the same candidates already reached by raw retrieval; the real bottleneck may be catalog absence or reranker choice rather than loss of variant provenance.","falsifier":"Among rows with canonical alternates, variant-aware fusion does not improve viable family/constraint-consistent candidate presence or rank, or it breaches public/hidden safety or coverage gates.","information_gain":"High. It tests whether accepted canonicalization has unrealized value because the current merger discards its second evidence signal, without repeating semantic expansion or catalog rewriting."},{"mechanism_family":"catalog_scope_and_request_intent","history_relation":"NEW_LAYER","causal_mechanism":"Use only affirmative combined evidence of service-only procurement or a requested product category absent from the LD taxonomy to expose uncertain/NOT_FOUND rather than force ordinary product selection; lines containing a purchasable product continue through normal retrieval.","competing_explanation":"Tender work descriptions can describe installation or repair alongside an intended LD product, so an intent route could create wrong NOT_FOUND outcomes and repeat earlier selection-adjacent regressions.","falsifier":"A manually reviewed non-benchmark sample shows substantial overlap between the proposed combined cues and viable LD product requests, or regression gates increase wrong-NOT_FOUND.","information_gain":"High. It directly distinguishes genuine catalog noncoverage from retrieval failure in a large real-tender class and tests the product goal’s uncertainty requirement."}]}
